Description: retro 2D karate game in a furnished apartment
 Karasheka is a retro karate game in which two karateka fight it out in
 an apartment: the living room, the kitchen, the bedroom and the study.
 Jump onto the furniture to get out of the way, then dive kick down on
 your opponent; light furniture breaks under a heavy landing.
 .
 Each fighter plays with nine direction keys, a strike key and a guard
 key. Every attack lands high, mid or low and is blocked only by the guard
 at that height. Play against the computer at three levels, against a
 second player on the same keyboard, or watch two computers fight.
 .
 All graphics and sound are generated by the game while it runs.
